      "amount": "",
      "notes": "fresh"
    },
    {
      "name": "1/4 cup chopped cilantro",
      "amount": "",
      "notes": "fresh"
    },
    {
      "name": "1/2 cup diced mango",
      "amount": "",
      "notes": "fresh"
    },
    {
      "name": "2 tablespoons lime juice",
      "amount": "",
      "notes": "freshly squeezed"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the shrimp under cold water and pat dry with paper towels.",
    "In a blender or food processor, combine coconut milk, honey, soy sauce, ginger, and lime juice. Blend until smooth.",
    "Add the chopped cilantro and blend until well combined.",
    "Cover a large plate or tray with parchment paper or a silicone mat.",
    "Place the shrimp on the prepared plate or tray in a single layer, leaving a little space between each shrimp.",
    "Pour the coconut milk mixture evenly over the shrimp.",
    "Garnish with diced mango and serve immediately.",
    "Alternatively, you can dehydrate the shrimp at 135°F (57°C) for 3-4 hours to create a crispy exterior and a juicy interior."
  ],
